w: Just as I am, Thine own to be, Friend of the young, who lov- est me,
w: In the glad morn- ing of my day, My life to give, my vows to pay,
w: I would live ev- er in the light, I would work ev- er for the right;
w: Just as I am, young, strong, and free, To be the best that I can be
w: With ma- ny dreams of fame and gold, Suc- cess and joy to make me bold,
w: And for Thy sake to win re- nown, And then to take the vic- tor’s crown,
